{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSetupError"],"title":"Sending to PostHog","anchor":"Sending-to-PostHog"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":") for your PostHog project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the project token and the host, posts to the host’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/batch\/"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splits each batch to PostHog’s limits (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"text":"). A batch with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The project token goes in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions enricher, also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record identifier. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"type":"text","text":". The record’s vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"properties ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":" and the like)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":" or is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, and one too large for PostHog’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event limit. The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reason is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"CollectorEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com or your own","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what PostHog receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"externalID":"PostHogEncoding","title":"PostHogEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic","title":"HTTPDestinations"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"postHog","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"projectToken","kind":"externalParam"},